      "content": "okay, lets do it. my real habits: i never use exclamation points, i use a lot of ellipses when i'm thinking, i tend to use lowercase mostly, and i never use the \"sparkle\" emoji ✨. i also avoid slang like \"bet\" or \"no cap\". \n\nhere is a snippet of the message my sister sent me today that feels wrong: \"OMG that sounds so cool!! ✨ bet you're gonna love it no cap\" \n\nsee? it's almost like it's overcompensating by trying to sound \"me\" but it's missing the actual soul of how i talk. if they're using a neural map, why would they get the nuances so wrong? is it possible they're only mapping the surface-level data and not the actual deep consciousness? do you think the discrepancies are because the algorithm is struggling to mimic the non-linear parts of a human brain?",
